   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( y = h(x) \\) be a solution of the differential equation \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = x^{3} - 17 x^{2} + 80 x - 100 \\), defined for \\( 0 < x < 9 \\). Find the value of \\( x \\) at which \\( h \\) has a relative minimum."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 2
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The differential equation gives the derivative directly: \\( h'(x) = x^{3} - 17 x^{2} + 80 x - 100 \\) for \\( 0 < x < 9 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               -10
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               -5
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               -2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Set \\( h'(x) = 0 \\) and factor: \\( (x - 2)(x - 5)(x - 10) = 0 \\), so \\( x = 2, 5, 10 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Only \\( x = 2 \\) and \\( x = 5 \\) lie in \\( 0 < x < 9 \\); \\( x = 10 \\) is outside the interval on which \\( h \\) is defined, so it is not a critical point of \\( h \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "\\( h' \\) changes from negative to positive at \\( x = 2 \\) and from positive to negative at \\( x = 5 \\), so \\( h \\) has its relative minimum at \\( x = 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      }
   ],
